# AI Research Orchestrator — Manifest

**Purpose:** Client-only PWA for agentic biomedical literature research: PubMed/NCBI, arXiv, multi-provider AI (Gemini / OpenAI / Anthropic / Ollama) or deterministic heuristic fallback, local Knowledge Base, and export — no application backend for user data.

**Stack:** React 19, TypeScript strict, Vite 8, Redux Toolkit, Dexie 4 + dexie-react-hooks (IndexedDB), Tailwind CSS v4, lazy provider SDKs, Marked/DOMPurify, jsPDF, **Recharts only**, Framer Motion, cmdk, Vitest + Testing Library, Playwright E2E (blocking Chromium + blocking Firefox/WebKit/mobile Chrome). Inference: `live | heuristic` (`src/services/nonAi/`, ADR 0007/0009).

**Architecture:** Browser talks directly to the selected AI provider + NCBI E-utilities (+ arXiv); AES-GCM keys via `apiKeyService`; Redux is the single source of truth; Context only hydrates/composes (`SettingsProvider`, KB) — never duplicate the same settings/UI flags. Synthesis trust: corpus-/claim-supported vs unverified narrative draft (ADR 0018). Cancelled/restored reports are `partial`, never `done` (ADR 0021).

**Conventions:** EN+DE via `t()` and `src/i18n/*Translations.ts` (drift-gated `productCopyPaths`); WCAG-oriented (ARIA, keyboard); new persistent data → Dexie schema in `databaseService` (current v7); Node **≥22**; `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`. Before commit: `typecheck` + `lint`; for core orchestration / Knowledge Base / `src/services` flows also run `pnpm run test:coverage` (or read the blocking CI coverage job). Prefer scoped Vitest/Playwright locally for unrelated UI edits; full coverage/E2E from CI. English-only new repo content (rule `010`). Charts: Recharts only. Do not reintroduce `lucide-react` or Chart.js.

**PR / CI gates (dual gate):** `docs/pr-merge-gate.md` + rules `011`/`013` — required CI green **and** review quiescence on the same latest head, including the **arrival wait** (do not merge while CodeAnt/Greptile/Copilot/CodeRabbit are still “Reviewing”). Always `@deepsourcebot review`; resolve bot threads and body-only findings; CodeRabbit rate-limit loop (bounded; optional-CR is Sourcery stand-in or the 2026-09-03 skip when Sourcery’s budget is exhausted). Do not `@sourcery-ai review` while the 250k / 7-day budget is exhausted. Blocking checks + PR-only `cancel-in-progress`: `docs/ci-branch-governance.md` + `docs/project-facts.json` (drift-gated). Live ruleset: `mainrules`.

**Modular rules:** `.cursor/rules/` — catalog in `000-cursor-rules.mdc` (`001` secrets, `010` English, `011`/`013` dual merge gate, `012` Dependabot, `100` providers/PubMed, `101` Dexie, `102` resilience, `200` file size, `300` UI, `800` tests, `850` notes/MCP).

**Standing deferrals:** Do not implement a first-class OpenRouter adapter (ADR 0010). Do not cut a ceremonial `v0.4.3`. Do not re-split the `geminiService` / `exportService` façades. Do not reintroduce `lucide-react` or Chart.js.

**Canonical:** `AGENTS.md`, `.github/copilot-instructions.md`, `README.md`, `docs/pr-merge-gate.md`, `docs/ci-branch-governance.md`, `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`.
